Hello! I’m Wahyu Zuli Firmanto, currently pursuing a Master of Public Policy at the Lee Kuan Yew School of Public Policy, National University of Singapore. My interests focus on labor, education, and development economics. Before joining the program, I worked for six years as Chief Marketing Officer at an education start-up in Indonesia, where I gained valuable insights into the private sector.

Outside of work and study, I’m passionate about giving back. I organized free classes and set up a street library for underprivileged children in my hometown, creating spaces for learning and growth.

This website is a place to record what I’m learning in public policy and showcase my portfolio. Thanks for visiting—hope you find something here that interests you!


